<% content_for :title, "Portfolio Performance" %>
<%
  labels = @period_defs.to_h
  trailing = %i[d1 w1 m1 m3 y1]
  calendar = %i[mtd qtd ytd]
  longterm = %i[inception]
  ordered  = trailing + calendar + longterm
  na_sort  = -99_999_999
  metric_val = ->(pr) { pr.available ? (@metric == "pnl" ? pr.pnl.to_f : pr.return_pct.to_f) : na_sort }
  risk_cols = [[:volatility, "Volatility"], [:sharpe, "Sharpe"], [:sortino, "Sortino"], [:max_drawdown, "Max DD"], [:calmar, "Calmar"]]
  rsort = ->(v) { v.nil? || v == :no_downside ? na_sort : v.to_f }
%>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
  <div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Portfolio Performance</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Time-weighted returns (Modified Dietz, daily-compounded). Deposits &amp; withdrawals are not counted as return. Values in <%= @reporting_currency&.code %>.</p>
  </div>
  <%= link_to "Back to portfolios", portfolios_path, class: "text-sm text-blue-600 hover:underline" %>
</div>

<%= form_with url: performance_portfolios_path, method: :get, data: { turbo_frame: "_top" }, class: "mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3 shadow-sm" do %>
  <div>
    <label class="block text-xs font-medium uppercase text-slate-500">Position role</label>
    <%= select_tag :position_role, options_for_select([["All", "all"], ["Base", "base"], ["Temporary", "temporary"]], @position_role), class: "mt-1 rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-2 text-sm" %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <label class="block text-xs font-medium uppercase text-slate-500">Show</label>
    <%= select_tag :metric, options_for_select([["Return %", "pct"], ["P&L (#{@reporting_currency&.code})", "pnl"]], @metric), class: "mt-1 rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-2 text-sm" %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <label class="block text-xs font-medium uppercase text-slate-500">Normalization</label>
    <%= select_tag :mode, options_for_select([["Own inception", "own"], ["Common start", "common"]], @chart_mode), class: "mt-1 rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-2 text-sm" %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <label class="block text-xs font-medium uppercase text-slate-500">Risk period</label>
    <%= select_tag :risk_period, options_for_select(PortfolioRiskService::RISK_PERIODS.map { |k, l| [l, k] }, @risk_period), class: "mt-1 rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-2 py-2 text-sm" %>
  </div>
  <div class="min-w-[16rem] flex-1">
    <label class="block text-xs font-medium uppercase text-slate-500">Portfolios <span class="font-normal normal-case text-slate-400">(none = all)</span></label>
    <div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
      <% @portfolios.each do |p| %>
        <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm">
          <%= check_box_tag "portfolio_ids[]", p.id, @selected_portfolio_ids.include?(p.id), class: "rounded border-slate-300" %>
          <span><%= p.name %></span>
        </label>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= submit_tag "Apply", class: "rounded-md bg-slate-800 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-white" %>
<% end %>

<% if @position_role != "all" %>
  <p class="mt-3 rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-amber-800">
    Showing <strong><%= @position_role.capitalize %></strong> exposure only. Filtered history is reconstructed from transaction lots (not by applying today's split to the past); where data is insufficient, periods show N/A.
  </p>
<% end %>

<%# Normalized comparison chart %>
<div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm"
     data-controller="perf-chart"
     data-perf-chart-url-value="<%= api_portfolios_performance_series_path %>"
     data-perf-chart-role-value="<%= @position_role %>"
     data-perf-chart-portfolio-ids-value="<%= @selected_portfolio_ids.join(',') %>"
     data-perf-chart-range-value="<%= @chart_range %>"
     data-perf-chart-mode-value="<%= @chart_mode %>"
     data-perf-chart-benchmark-value="<%= @chart_benchmark %>">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
    <h2 class="font-medium text-slate-900">Normalized comparison <span class="text-xs font-normal text-slate-400">(compounded returns · start = 100)</span></h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1 text-xs">
      <% %w[1m qtd 3m 6m ytd 1y all].each do |r| %>
        <button type="button" data-perf-chart-target="rangeButton" data-action="perf-chart#setRange" data-range="<%= r %>"
                class="rounded px-2 py-1 font-medium <%= @chart_range == r ? 'bg-blue-600 text-white' : 'bg-slate-100 text-slate-700' %>"><%= r.upcase %></button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1">
      <span class="text-xs font-medium uppercase text-slate-500">View</span>
      <button type="button" data-perf-chart-target="viewButton" data-action="perf-chart#setView" data-view="index" class="rounded px-2 py-1 text-xs font-medium bg-blue-600 text-white">Index</button>
      <button type="button" data-perf-chart-target="viewButton" data-action="perf-chart#setView" data-view="drawdown" class="rounded px-2 py-1 text-xs font-medium bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">Drawdown</button>
    </div>
    <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
      <input type="checkbox" <%= "checked" if @chart_benchmark %> data-action="perf-chart#toggleBenchmark" class="rounded border-slate-300">
      <span>Show benchmarks</span>
    </label>
    <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">Normalization: <strong><%= @chart_mode == "common" ? "Common start" : "Own inception" %></strong> (change above)</span>
    <p data-perf-chart-target="commonNote" hidden class="text-xs text-slate-500"></p>
  </div>

  <p data-perf-chart-target="empty" hidden class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">N/A — insufficient historical data to chart the selected portfolios.</p>
  <div class="mt-3" style="height:20rem"><canvas data-perf-chart-target="canvas"></canvas></div>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-400">Own inception: each series starts at 100 on its own first snapshot. Common start: all series (and benchmarks) rebased to 100 on the latest inception among the selected portfolios — the fair same-period comparison.</p>
</div>

<%# Risk summary cards + risk-vs-return scatter %>
<% prisks = @rows.select { |r| r.scope.is_a?(Portfolio) && @risk_by_row&.dig(r.scope.id) }.map { |r| [r, @risk_by_row[r.scope.id]] } %>
<% best = ->(sel) { cand = prisks.map { |r, rk| [r, sel.call(rk)] }.reject { |_r, v| v.nil? || v == :no_downside }; cand.max_by { |_r, v| v.to_f } } %>
<% least_dd = ->{ cand = prisks.map { |r, rk| [r, rk.max_drawdown] }.reject { |_r, v| v.nil? }; cand.max_by { |_r, v| v.to_f } } %>
<% cards = [
     ["Best return", best.call(->(rk){ rk.total_return }), :ret],
     ["Best Sharpe", best.call(->(rk){ rk.sharpe }), :ratio],
     ["Best Sortino", best.call(->(rk){ rk.sortino }), :ratio],
     ["Lowest drawdown", least_dd.call, :dd],
     ["Best Calmar", best.call(->(rk){ rk.calmar }), :ratio]
   ] %>
<% if prisks.any? && cards.any? { |_l, pair, _k| pair } %>
  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5">
    <% cards.each do |label, pair, kind| %>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3 shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500"><%= label %></p>
        <% if pair %>
          <p class="mt-1 truncate text-sm font-medium text-slate-800" title="<%= pair[0].label %>"><%= pair[0].label %></p>
          <p class="mt-0.5 text-lg font-semibold tabular-nums">
            <% v = pair[1] %>
            <% case kind %>
            <% when :ret %><span class="<%= pnl_class_for(v * 100) %>"><%= format_upside(v.to_d * 100) %></span>
            <% when :dd %><%= risk_drawdown(v) %>
            <% else %><%= number_with_precision(v, precision: 2) %>
            <% end %>
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-300">N/A</p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<% scatter_pts = prisks.filter_map { |r, rk| { label: r.label, x: (rk.volatility ? (rk.volatility * 100).to_f.round(2) : nil), y: (rk.annualized_return ? (rk.annualized_return * 100).to_f.round(2) : nil) } if rk.volatility && rk.annualized_return } %>
<% if scatter_pts.size >= 1 %>
  <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm" data-controller="risk-scatter" data-risk-scatter-points-value="<%= scatter_pts.to_json %>">
    <h2 class="font-medium text-slate-900">Risk vs return <span class="text-xs font-normal text-slate-400">(annualized)</span></h2>
    <div class="mt-3" style="height:18rem"><canvas data-risk-scatter-target="canvas"></canvas></div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-400">X = annualized volatility · Y = annualized return. Upper-left is better (more return per unit of risk). Only portfolios with ≥90 days of history appear.</p>
  </div>
<% end %>

<%# Grouped period table %>
<div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
  <table data-controller="sortable-table" class="min-w-[52rem] w-full text-left text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">
      <tr>
        <th colspan="2" class="px-4 py-2"></th>
        <th colspan="5" class="border-l border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-center">Trailing returns</th>
        <th colspan="3" class="border-l border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-center">Calendar returns</th>
        <th colspan="1" class="border-l border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-center">Long term</th>
        <th colspan="5" class="border-l-2 border-slate-300 px-4 py-2 text-center">Risk &amp; efficiency</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="sticky left-0 z-10 w-44 min-w-[11rem] bg-slate-50 px-4 py-2">Portfolio</th>
        <th class="sticky left-44 z-10 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-2 text-right">Value</th>
        <% ordered.each_with_index do |k, i| %>
          <th class="px-4 py-2 text-right <%= 'border-l border-slate-200' if [0, 5, 8].include?(i) %>" data-sort-value=""><%= labels[k] %></th>
        <% end %>
        <% risk_cols.each_with_index do |(k, label), i| %>
          <th class="px-4 py-2 text-right <%= i.zero? ? 'border-l-2 border-slate-300' : '' %>"><%= label %></th>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @rows.each do |row| %>
        <% combined = row.scope == :combined %>
        <% bm = row.scope.is_a?(Portfolio) ? @benchmark_by_portfolio_id[row.scope.id] : nil %>
        <tr class="border-t border-slate-100 <%= 'bg-slate-50 font-medium' if combined %>">
          <td class="sticky left-0 z-10 w-44 min-w-[11rem] px-4 py-3 <%= combined ? 'bg-slate-50 font-medium' : 'bg-white' %>" data-sort-value="<%= row.label %>">
            <% if row.scope.is_a?(Portfolio) %>
              <%= link_to row.label, row.scope, class: "text-blue-600 hover:underline" %>
            <% else %>
              <%= row.label %>
            <% end %>
            <% if row.inception %>
              <span class="block text-[11px] font-normal text-slate-400" title="First valid performance snapshot">Since <%= l row.inception %></span>
            <% end %>
            <% if bm %>
              <details class="mt-1">
                <summary class="cursor-pointer text-[11px] font-normal text-blue-600">vs <%= bm[:index].code %></summary>
                <table class="mt-1 text-[11px] tabular-nums">
                  <% %i[m1 m3 qtd ytd y1 inception].each do |key| %>
                    <% b = bm[:returns][key]; pr = row.periods[key] %>
                    <% alpha = (pr&.available && b) ? (pr.return_pct - b) : nil %>
                    <tr>
                      <td class="pr-2 text-slate-500"><%= labels[key] %></td>
                      <td class="pr-2 text-right text-slate-500">bench <%= b ? format_upside(b) : "—" %></td>
                      <td class="text-right">α <% if alpha %><span class="<%= pnl_class_for(alpha) %>"><%= format_upside(alpha) %></span><% else %><span class="text-slate-300">N/A</span><% end %></td>
                    </tr>
                  <% end %>
                </table>
              </details>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="sticky left-44 z-10 px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums <%= combined ? 'bg-slate-50 font-medium' : 'bg-white' %>" data-sort-value="<%= row.current_value.to_f %>">
            <%= row.current_value ? number_with_precision(row.current_value, precision: 0) : "—" %>
          </td>
          <% ordered.each_with_index do |key, i| %>
            <% pr = row.periods[key] %>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums <%= 'border-l border-slate-100' if [0, 5, 8].include?(i) %>" data-sort-value="<%= metric_val.call(pr) %>">
              <% if !pr.available %>
                <span class="text-slate-300" title="Insufficient history">N/A</span>
              <% elsif @metric == "pnl" %>
                <span class="<%= pnl_class_for(pr.pnl) %>"><%= format_pnl_value(pr.pnl, precision: 0) %></span>
              <% else %>
                <span class="<%= pnl_class_for(pr.return_pct) %>"><%= format_upside(pr.return_pct) %></span>
              <% end %>
              <% if key == :d1 && pr.available %>
                <span class="ml-1 rounded px-1 text-[9px] font-medium <%= row.final ? 'bg-slate-100 text-slate-500' : 'bg-amber-50 text-amber-700' %>" title="<%= row.final ? 'End-of-day snapshot' : 'Value not yet finalized for today' %>"><%= row.final ? "Final" : "Intraday" %></span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
          <% rk = row.scope.is_a?(Portfolio) ? row.scope.id : (row.scope == :combined ? :combined : nil) %>
          <% risk = rk && @risk_by_row ? @risk_by_row[rk] : nil %>
          <% risk_cols.each_with_index do |(k, _label), i| %>
            <% v = risk&.public_send(k) %>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums <%= i.zero? ? 'border-l-2 border-slate-200' : '' %>" data-sort-value="<%= rsort.call(v) %>">
              <% if risk.nil? %>
                <span class="text-slate-300" title="Insufficient history">N/A</span>
              <% elsif k == :volatility %>
                <%= risk_pct(v) %>
              <% elsif k == :max_drawdown %>
                <%= risk_drawdown(v) %>
              <% else %>
                <%= risk_ratio(v) %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <% if @rows.all? { |r| r.current_value.nil? } %>
        <tr><td colspan="16" class="px-4 py-6 text-center text-slate-500">No snapshot history yet. Values accrue daily; historical periods fill in as snapshots (or a reconstruction backfill) become available.</td></tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 text-xs text-slate-400">
  <span><strong>Trailing</strong> 1D/1W/1M/3M/1Y need a snapshot at/before the period start, else N/A.</span>
  <span><strong>Calendar</strong> MTD/QTD/YTD anchor at the period start or inception (3M ≠ QTD, 1Y ≠ YTD).</span>
  <span><strong>Long term</strong> compounds the full history.</span>
  <span>Internal portfolio-to-portfolio moves net out in “All portfolios”.</span>
</div>

<div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-4 text-xs text-slate-600">
  <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-slate-700">Risk &amp; efficiency — how these are computed</p>
  <p>All risk metrics use the same cash-flow-adjusted daily returns as the table, over the selected <strong>Risk period</strong> (<%= PortfolioRiskService::RISK_PERIODS.to_h[@risk_period] %>) and, in Common start mode, the shared window — so deposits, withdrawals and internal transfers create no artificial volatility or drawdown. Risk-free rate used: <strong><%= number_with_precision(@risk_free_pct, precision: 2) %>% annual</strong> (<%= link_to "change", edit_settings_analytics_setting_path, class: "text-blue-600 hover:underline" %>).</p>
  <ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5">
    <li><strong>Volatility</strong> — annualized standard deviation of daily returns (σ·√252). Neutral: neither good nor bad on its own.</li>
    <li><strong>Sharpe</strong> — excess return (over the risk-free rate) per unit of total volatility.</li>
    <li><strong>Sortino</strong> — excess return per unit of <em>downside</em> volatility only.</li>
    <li><strong>Max drawdown</strong> — largest peak-to-trough decline of the compounded return index over the period.</li>
    <li><strong>Calmar</strong> — annualized return ÷ |max drawdown|. Shown only with ≥90 days of history.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-2">Minimum history before a value is shown: Volatility 20 days · Sharpe/Sortino 30 days · Max DD 5 days · Calmar 90 days. Below that, the cell reads N/A rather than an annualized, misleading number. Interpretation depends on the market and period — treat these as analytical inputs, not verdicts.</p>
</div>
